 questions the trustworthiness of the author. An active reader doesn’t passively sponge up information, but uses the author’s argument as a springboard for critical thought and deep understanding." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.bharatisethiya.explorableexplanations" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[45,560][963,938]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /><node index="4" text="A typical book or website displays the author’s argument, and nothing else. We form questions, but can’t answer them. We consider alternatives, but can’t explore them. We question assumptions, but can’t verify them." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.bharatisethiya.explorableexplanations" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[45,979][963,1249]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /><node index="5" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="com.bharatisethiya.explorableexplanations" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[45,1290][963,1542]" drawing-order="0" hint=""><node index="0" text="The goal is to change people’s relationship with text: from information to be consumed into an environment to think in." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.bharatisethiya.explorableexplanations" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[90,1335][918,1497]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /></node><nod